      "knowledgePoint": {
        "id": 17592186172086,
        "title": "Finding the Domain of a Vector Field"
      },
      "markdown": "Determine the domain of the real vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}\\,i+\\left(y^{2}\\right)\\,j.\n$$\n\nRemember: both component functions must be defined.",
      "mathAcademyId": null,
      "requiresCalculator": null,
      "solution": "Write $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y)&=\\frac{1}{x}\\\\Q(x,y)&=y^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nP: Every denominator must be nonzero, including a square root in a denominator.\n\nThe required conditions are $x \\neq 0$.\n\nThus $D_P=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x \\neq 0\\right\\}$.\n\nQ: This polynomial is defined everywhere in the real plane.\n\nThus $D_Q=\\mathbb R^2$.\n\nThe domain is the intersection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D&=D_P\\cap D_Q\\\\&=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x \\neq 0\\right\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "status": "correct",
